<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">12</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-bi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Bi</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 597 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Bi was fought in 597 BCE near the Yellow River in modern Henan, when King Zhuang of Chu defeated an army of Jin that had come to relieve the State of Zheng.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-an"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-an.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of An</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 589 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of An was fought in 589 BCE in modern Shandong, when the State of Jin and its allies Lu and Wey defeated the State of Qi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-yanling"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-yanling.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Yanling</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 575 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Yanling was fought in 575 BCE in modern Henan between the State of Jin and the State of Chu, which had come to support Zheng.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-irasa"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Irasa</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 570 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Irasa was fought around 570 BCE in Cyrenaica, in present-day Libya, where the Greeks of Cyrene under Battus II defeated an Egyptian army sent by the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-fetters"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-fetters.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Fetters</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 560 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Fetters was fought in the 6th century BCE between Sparta and the Arcadian city of Tegea.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pteria"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Pteria</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 547 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Pteria was fought around 547 BCE in Cappadocia, east of the Halys river, between Croesus of Lydia and Cyrus the Great of Persia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pallene"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Pallene</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 546 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Pallene was fought in Attica around 546 BCE, when Peisistratus, returning from exile with mercenaries and allies, surprised and routed the Athenian forces…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-champions"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Champions</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 546 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Champions was fought about 546 BCE between Sparta and Argos for the border district of Thyreatis.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-thymbra"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-thymbra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Thymbra</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 546 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Thymbra was fought in 546 BCE in western Anatolia, where Cyrus the Great defeated Croesus of Lydia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-opis"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Opis</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 539 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Opis was fought in 539 BCE near the Tigris in Mesopotamia, where the Persian forces of Cyrus the Great defeated the Babylonian army.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pelusium"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-pelusium.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Pelusium</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 525 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Pelusium was fought in 525 BCE at the eastern edge of the Nile Delta, where the Persian king Cambyses II defeated Pharaoh Psamtik III.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-boju"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-boju.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Boju</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 506 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Boju was fought in 506 BCE in modern Hubei, when King Helü of Wu, advised by the Chu exile Wu Zixu and traditionally by Sun Wu, invaded Chu and defeated…</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Sieges <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-jerusalem-597-bce"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Jerusalem (597 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 597 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Jerusalem in 597 BCE was the capture of Jerusalem by Nebuchadnezzar II of the Chaldean Empire after the kingdom of Judah rebelled.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-jerusalem-587-bce"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Jerusalem (587 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 587 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Jerusalem in 587 BCE was the capture and destruction of Jerusalem by the Chaldean (Neo-Babylonian) king Nebuchadnezzar II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-tyre-585-572-bce"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Tyre (585–572 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · c. 585 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Tyre was a long siege of the Phoenician island city of Tyre by Nebuchadnezzar II of the Chaldean Empire, begun c. 585 BCE.</span></a></li></ul></section>
